{title: 488 - At First I Prayed for Light}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #488 • WOOLWICH • 12.14}
{lyricist: Mrs. E. D. Cheney}
{composer: C. E. Kettle}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 488}
{meta: tune WOOLWICH}
{meta: meter 12.14}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]At first I [C/G]prayed [G]for [D7]light: Could I but see [Em]the [G7/F]way,
[G7/F]How gladly, [G/D]swiftly [C]would I [Em]walk To [D]everlasting [G]day!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]And next I [D7]prayed for [Em]strength:
[G]That I might [D7]tread the [Em]road
[G7/F]With [C/E]firm, [G/D]unfaltering [D7]feet, and win
[G7/F]The [C/E]heaven's serene [D7]abode.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]And then I [D7]asked for [Em]faith:
[G]Could I but [D7]trust my [Em]God,
[G7/F]I'd [C/E]live infolded [D]in [D7]His peace,
[G7/F]Though [G/D]foes [C]were [Em]all [D7]abroad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]But now I [D7]pray for [Em]love:
[G]Deep love to [D7]God and [Em]man;
[G7/F]A [C/E]living love [Em]that [D]will [D7]not fail,
[G7/F]However [Em]dark [D7]His plan.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]And light and [D7]strength and [Em]faith
[G]Are opening [D7]everywhere!
[G7/F]God [C/E]waited patiently [D7]until
[G7/F]I [G/D]prayed [C]the [Em]larger [D7]prayer.
{end_of_verse}
